1
00:01:30,990 --> 00:01:33,990
Ugh, is this even the right way?

2
00:01:33,990 --> 00:01:34,990
It definitely is.

3
00:01:34,990 --> 00:01:36,990
Are you sure?

4
00:01:38,990 --> 00:01:39,990
Stop!

5
00:01:39,990 --> 00:01:40,990
Pick up the pace!

6
00:01:40,990 --> 00:01:41,990
Tell that to the others!

7
00:01:41,990 --> 00:01:43,990
Hey now, don't push!

8
00:01:47,990 --> 00:01:50,990
I remembered this all.

9
00:01:50,990 --> 00:01:52,990
This is where we fought the Red Dragon.

10
00:01:54,990 --> 00:01:55,990
I see.

11
00:01:55,990 --> 00:01:58,990
So you came all the way out here on your last expedition?

12
00:01:58,990 --> 00:01:59,990
Yeah.

13
00:01:59,990 --> 00:02:03,990
This was thought to be the deepest part of the dungeon for a while.

14
00:02:03,990 --> 00:02:07,990
But recently, someone found a door around here that seems to lead farther in.

15
00:02:07,990 --> 00:02:11,990
There were patterns engraved on it, so it was thought to open with magic.

16
00:02:11,990 --> 00:02:15,990
The Island Lord asked us to come copy the patterns for him, but then...

17
00:02:18,990 --> 00:02:21,990
You ran into the Red Dragon and eventually had to retreat.

18
00:02:23,990 --> 00:02:24,990
Alright, let's test our luck.

19
00:02:24,990 --> 00:02:27,990
I think we were around there last time.

20
00:02:29,990 --> 00:02:30,990
Hey!

21
00:02:30,990 --> 00:02:31,990
Found our stuff!

22
00:02:31,990 --> 00:02:32,990
Huh?

23
00:02:32,990 --> 00:02:33,990
It's been ransacked.

24
00:02:33,990 --> 00:02:34,990
Oh no!

25
00:02:37,990 --> 00:02:38,990
Heck yeah!

26
00:02:38,990 --> 00:02:39,990
I found my sleeping bag!

27
00:02:39,990 --> 00:02:40,990
Thank God!

28
00:02:40,990 --> 00:02:41,990
My underwear survived!

29
00:02:41,990 --> 00:02:44,990
You checked for that stuff first instead of money, huh?

30
00:02:44,990 --> 00:02:47,990
It seems like all the food we had was taken.

31
00:02:47,990 --> 00:02:49,990
But everything else is here.

32
00:02:49,990 --> 00:02:51,990
Safe to assume monsters did this.

33
00:02:51,990 --> 00:02:52,990
This is great!

34
00:02:52,990 --> 00:02:54,990
Now I'll be all warm when I fall off!

35
00:02:58,990 --> 00:02:59,990
That's bad.

36
00:02:59,990 --> 00:03:02,990
Let's find a place where we can rest for a bit.

37
00:03:02,990 --> 00:03:04,990
Gives me time to sort my things.

38
00:03:04,990 --> 00:03:07,990
I wonder if the snow makes the cleaners slow down at all.

39
00:03:07,990 --> 00:03:09,990
Something nibbled on my soul!

40
00:03:09,990 --> 00:03:10,990
Hey you!

41
00:03:10,990 --> 00:03:12,990
Remove whatever you just put in your pocket.

42
00:03:16,990 --> 00:03:17,990
Hey Marcel, catch!

43
00:03:17,990 --> 00:03:18,990
Huh?

44
00:03:18,990 --> 00:03:21,990
You're not really well trained for a beast man.

45
00:03:21,990 --> 00:03:24,990
I'm starting to realize where they'd probably put that collar on you.

46
00:03:25,990 --> 00:03:27,990
You're one of those half-foots, I'm assuming.

47
00:03:27,990 --> 00:03:30,990
I'd only just heard of them since there aren't any in the East.

48
00:03:30,990 --> 00:03:32,990
I'd never seen one till coming here.

49
00:03:33,990 --> 00:03:35,990
The name of your race is pretty strange.

50
00:03:35,990 --> 00:03:40,990
I heard it came from your kind getting one of their legs chopped off due to committing too much thievery.

51
00:03:40,990 --> 00:03:43,990
Come on you two, there's no need for that.

52
00:03:45,990 --> 00:03:46,990
Marcel!

53
00:03:46,990 --> 00:03:47,990
Come here!

54
00:03:50,990 --> 00:03:52,990
Oh, you found fish!

55
00:03:52,990 --> 00:03:55,990
Is there a way for us to cut out this uncovered part right here?

56
00:03:56,990 --> 00:03:59,990
I could maybe do it with a magic circle.

57
00:03:59,990 --> 00:04:00,990
That's right!

58
00:04:00,990 --> 00:04:01,990
Do you want to give it a try?

59
00:04:01,990 --> 00:04:04,990
I can teach you how to draw one if you do.

60
00:04:05,990 --> 00:04:07,990
How's your mana sickness been lately?

61
00:04:07,990 --> 00:04:09,990
I haven't been staggering as much.

62
00:04:09,990 --> 00:04:12,990
The hallucinations have gotten a lot worse though.

63
00:04:13,990 --> 00:04:16,990
I caught this fish a lot on the fourth floor.

64
00:04:17,990 --> 00:04:21,990
Is the water flowing in from the upper floors freezing once it gets down here?

65
00:04:22,990 --> 00:04:24,990
Seems a lot of stuff got washed up in this place.

66
00:04:27,990 --> 00:04:28,990
And that completes the circle.

67
00:04:29,990 --> 00:04:30,990
How are you feeling?

68
00:04:30,990 --> 00:04:32,990
A bit tired honestly.

69
00:04:32,990 --> 00:04:34,990
Well, let me activate it then.

70
00:04:34,990 --> 00:04:36,990
All you've got to do is...

71
00:04:36,990 --> 00:04:39,990
Imagine water filling these symbols and...

72
00:04:42,990 --> 00:04:43,990
What's this?

73
00:04:43,990 --> 00:04:45,990
The floor's moving!

74
00:04:49,990 --> 00:04:50,990
A monster!

75
00:04:50,990 --> 00:04:51,990
There?

76
00:04:51,990 --> 00:04:52,990
That thing is an ice golem.

77
00:04:52,990 --> 00:04:53,990
Hmm...

78
00:04:56,990 --> 00:04:57,990
I see.

79
00:05:04,990 --> 00:05:05,990
Above you!

80
00:05:05,990 --> 00:05:06,990
Look out!

81
00:05:09,990 --> 00:05:10,990
My house!

82
00:05:20,990 --> 00:05:21,990
There's a fish!

83
00:05:21,990 --> 00:05:22,990
There's a fish!

84
00:05:22,990 --> 00:05:23,990
There's too much crap in it!

85
00:05:23,990 --> 00:05:24,990
Hey, uh...

86
00:05:24,990 --> 00:05:25,990
How do I kill this big snowman?

87
00:05:25,990 --> 00:05:27,990
It's a golem, so you're gonna have to destroy its core!

88
00:05:27,990 --> 00:05:28,990
Core?

89
00:05:28,990 --> 00:05:29,990
Where would that even...

90
00:05:29,990 --> 00:05:30,990
Where would that even...

91
00:05:38,990 --> 00:05:39,990
Well?

92
00:05:39,990 --> 00:05:40,990
Where is it?

93
00:05:40,990 --> 00:05:41,990
Give me a sec!

94
00:05:41,990 --> 00:05:42,990
Is that it?

95
00:05:42,990 --> 00:05:43,990
No, that's a fish.

96
00:05:44,990 --> 00:05:45,990
Yeah, there's too much crap in it!

97
00:05:46,990 --> 00:05:47,990
Hey!

98
00:05:47,990 --> 00:05:49,990
Try to distract the enemy to buy me time!

99
00:05:49,990 --> 00:05:50,990
I still need to find the car!

100
00:05:50,990 --> 00:05:51,990
Huh?!

101
00:05:52,990 --> 00:05:53,990
That bastard.

102
00:05:53,990 --> 00:05:54,990
How do I know he's not lying?

103
00:05:54,990 --> 00:05:56,990
This better not be a trick or something.

104
00:05:59,990 --> 00:06:00,990
The snow!

105
00:06:03,990 --> 00:06:04,990
The snow!

106
00:06:15,990 --> 00:06:16,990
Why'd it stop moving?

107
00:06:16,990 --> 00:06:17,990
Look!

108
00:06:29,990 --> 00:06:30,990
Can you hurry?

109
00:06:30,990 --> 00:06:31,990
How long do I have to keep this up?

110
00:06:31,990 --> 00:06:32,990
You're good!

111
00:06:32,990 --> 00:06:33,990
That was long enough!

112
00:06:39,990 --> 00:06:40,990
Yes!

113
00:06:40,990 --> 00:06:41,990
Nailed it!

114
00:06:42,990 --> 00:06:43,990
Idiot!

115
00:06:43,990 --> 00:06:44,990
Do you think this is a game?

116
00:06:44,990 --> 00:06:45,990
You're the idiots!

117
00:06:45,990 --> 00:06:46,990
Check out!

118
00:06:46,990 --> 00:06:47,990
We're the hero idiots!

119
00:06:50,990 --> 00:06:51,990
By the way!

120
00:06:51,990 --> 00:06:53,990
While I am able to use ranged weapons,

121
00:06:53,990 --> 00:06:56,990
I can't exactly do that much damage with any of them!

122
00:06:56,990 --> 00:06:58,990
So you better not go counting on me in a fight!

123
00:06:58,990 --> 00:06:59,990
The rest is up to you!

124
00:07:03,990 --> 00:07:04,990
Fine.

125
00:07:05,990 --> 00:07:07,990
As long as I know how to kill it.

126
00:07:07,990 --> 00:07:22,990
It looks like I'm the only one in the group who's agile enough to take on an enemy that big!

127
00:07:22,990 --> 00:07:23,990
Can't believe how slow you guys are!

128
00:07:23,990 --> 00:07:24,990
I...

129
00:07:24,990 --> 00:07:25,990
I...

130
00:07:25,990 --> 00:07:26,990
I...

131
00:07:26,990 --> 00:07:27,990
I...

132
00:07:27,990 --> 00:07:28,990
I...

133
00:07:28,990 --> 00:07:29,990
I...

134
00:07:29,990 --> 00:07:30,990
I...

135
00:07:30,990 --> 00:07:31,990
I...

136
00:07:31,990 --> 00:07:39,990
I...

137
00:07:39,990 --> 00:07:40,990
I....

138
00:07:40,990 --> 00:07:41,990
I...

139
00:07:41,990 --> 00:07:42,990
I...

140
00:07:42,990 --> 00:07:43,990
I...

141
00:07:43,990 --> 00:07:44,990
I...

142
00:07:44,990 --> 00:07:45,990
I...

143
00:07:45,990 --> 00:07:46,990
Are all of you doing ok?

144
00:07:46,990 --> 00:07:47,990
It'll start to warm up soon!

145
00:07:47,990 --> 00:07:54,390
Okay, it'll start to warm up soon. That magic circle will get hot, so please be careful not to burn yourselves.

146
00:07:54,630 --> 00:08:00,610
Take off all your wet clothes so we can dry them. That means you too. Here, I'll hold this up to cover you.

147
00:08:01,290 --> 00:08:02,810
Do you need help with yours, Laios?

148
00:08:04,650 --> 00:08:06,330
Could one of you guys help him out?

149
00:08:07,650 --> 00:08:10,130
You really don't have to do that, you know.

150
00:08:10,710 --> 00:08:12,370
No, it's not that big of a deal.

151
00:08:17,990 --> 00:08:24,770
Not like anyone's gonna get excited over a beast getting naked.

152
00:08:25,630 --> 00:08:27,090
What the hell are you doing?

153
00:08:27,210 --> 00:08:29,530
Well, it would be bad if you felt colder.

154
00:08:29,890 --> 00:08:32,930
At least tell me the number of nipples and where the tail connection is...

155
00:08:32,930 --> 00:08:42,310
It's finally gotten warmer in here. I'll start fixing up a hot meal for everyone.

156
00:08:43,450 --> 00:08:45,290
But first, I need to thaw this.

157
00:08:45,290 --> 00:08:48,190
Might as well melt it with the magic circle.

158
00:08:51,490 --> 00:08:52,790
Must have been too close.

159
00:08:53,070 --> 00:08:55,970
Wow, but this is actually nice. It's like a sauna.

160
00:08:56,410 --> 00:09:00,330
We haven't been able to take a bath for a while, so let's sweat it out a little bit.

161
00:09:05,510 --> 00:09:07,050
Wait, that comes off?

162
00:09:07,370 --> 00:09:08,490
Why is it only me?

163
00:09:09,190 --> 00:09:12,010
Gut the fish and then make a broth from the head and bones.

164
00:09:12,390 --> 00:09:15,050
I feel like we're gonna smell like fish after this.

165
00:09:15,290 --> 00:09:18,010
Finally, slice a couple mushrooms and nightmares.

166
00:09:18,750 --> 00:09:22,210
Lightly boil the shapeshifter meat and remove any scum that forms.

167
00:09:22,810 --> 00:09:27,370
Beat some harpy eggs and then add that mixture to the broth along with all the other ingredients.

168
00:09:30,730 --> 00:09:32,210
Pour all that into cups.

169
00:09:33,070 --> 00:09:36,970
Place the cups into the pan with ice golem fragments and put over a fire.

170
00:09:36,970 --> 00:09:39,990
Look, I made this from her fur.

171
00:09:40,430 --> 00:09:41,190
Bored much?

172
00:09:41,550 --> 00:09:44,390
Lastly, place some mandrake leaves over the top and...

173
00:09:45,030 --> 00:09:45,890
It's red...

174
00:09:45,890 --> 00:09:47,030
Hey!

175
00:09:47,630 --> 00:09:49,370
Don't just start eating on your own.

176
00:09:49,770 --> 00:09:52,250
You've gotta wait until everyone gathers at the table.

177
00:09:52,570 --> 00:09:53,450
Why should I wait?

178
00:09:53,590 --> 00:09:55,690
I defeated that thing all by myself!

179
00:09:55,690 --> 00:09:58,410
I think I deserve to eat before the rest of you!

180
00:09:58,410 --> 00:10:01,430
A meal's something you only start when everyone's together.

181
00:10:02,150 --> 00:10:02,570
Chill, Chuck.

182
00:10:02,790 --> 00:10:03,750
Lios is outside.

183
00:10:04,130 --> 00:10:05,250
Mind calling him back in?

184
00:10:05,490 --> 00:10:06,050
Sure thing.

185
00:10:07,090 --> 00:10:08,970
Oh, this feels great.

186
00:10:09,090 --> 00:10:10,310
Is this guy for real?

187
00:10:10,310 --> 00:10:17,790
Now that everyone's gathered, I think it's that time.

188
00:10:18,150 --> 00:10:19,090
So let's eat!

189
00:10:19,690 --> 00:10:20,750
Let's read it in!

190
00:10:22,230 --> 00:10:23,230
It's pudding.

191
00:10:24,610 --> 00:10:24,950
Oops!

192
00:10:25,210 --> 00:10:26,050
Sorry, Marcel.

193
00:10:26,310 --> 00:10:26,830
Delicious!

194
00:10:27,890 --> 00:10:29,450
What a waste of time.

195
00:10:29,750 --> 00:10:30,890
Hey, Yuzutsumi.

196
00:10:31,230 --> 00:10:32,030
What is it?

197
00:10:32,410 --> 00:10:33,310
This is for you.

198
00:10:34,190 --> 00:10:36,150
I sewed up one of the bags that got ripped.

199
00:10:36,510 --> 00:10:37,230
You should use it.

200
00:10:40,310 --> 00:10:43,870
And, uh, I'm sorry I called you a beast before.

201
00:10:44,470 --> 00:10:46,310
I have a notoriously foul mouth.

202
00:10:47,310 --> 00:10:50,730
You know, traveling with a group of strangers can be uncomfortable.

203
00:10:51,670 --> 00:10:54,230
But once you get used to it, you'll see the advantages.

204
00:10:55,250 --> 00:10:57,630
You can rely on them to handle things for you.

205
00:10:59,230 --> 00:10:59,670
Um...

206
00:10:59,670 --> 00:11:01,670
Uh...

207
00:11:01,670 --> 00:11:07,870
Thank you for the good meal!

208
00:11:09,550 --> 00:11:10,070
Thanks.

209
00:11:10,310 --> 00:11:14,550
Come on, are you done yet?

210
00:11:14,930 --> 00:11:15,370
Almost.

211
00:11:15,790 --> 00:11:16,570
Just a second.

212
00:11:17,270 --> 00:11:19,990
This goes here, and...

213
00:11:19,990 --> 00:11:20,330
Done!

214
00:11:21,670 --> 00:11:22,250
Ta-da!

215
00:11:25,250 --> 00:11:27,690
Their Namaari's close, but they're perfect, right?

216
00:11:27,850 --> 00:11:29,070
It's hard to move.

217
00:11:29,370 --> 00:11:31,550
It did take a while to take them in, though.

218
00:11:31,790 --> 00:11:33,190
Yeah, now I'm cold again.

219
00:11:33,430 --> 00:11:34,390
Look, I'm sorry.

220
00:11:34,730 --> 00:11:35,970
Let's start heading out now.

221
00:11:36,110 --> 00:11:36,630
Hold on.

222
00:11:38,690 --> 00:11:39,250
Great.

223
00:11:39,250 --> 00:11:41,810
I boiled the mandrakes in some sweet sauce.

224
00:11:42,450 --> 00:11:44,690
Figured it'd be a good thing to snack on while we walked.

225
00:11:44,690 --> 00:11:49,570
Hey.

226
00:11:51,250 --> 00:11:51,770
Here.

227
00:11:53,650 --> 00:11:55,250
But this belongs to you.

228
00:11:56,070 --> 00:11:57,030
Don't want it.

229
00:11:57,710 --> 00:11:58,110
Why?

230
00:11:58,430 --> 00:11:59,590
It's really good.

231
00:11:59,990 --> 00:12:01,730
I said I don't want the thing!

232
00:12:01,730 --> 00:12:02,430
Oh, come on.

233
00:12:02,490 --> 00:12:03,670
Just try a little bite.

234
00:12:03,890 --> 00:12:04,330
Here.

235
00:12:04,630 --> 00:12:05,570
Cut it now!

236
00:12:08,290 --> 00:12:09,370
Oh, horrible.

237
00:12:09,790 --> 00:12:12,590
We've been walking for two seconds, and there's already blood drawn.

238
00:12:12,770 --> 00:12:14,090
Hey, just leave her be.

239
00:12:14,330 --> 00:12:15,470
She'll eat when she gets hungry.

240
00:12:15,470 --> 00:12:18,210
So why don't you want to eat it?

241
00:12:18,530 --> 00:12:19,470
It's a monster.

242
00:12:19,810 --> 00:12:21,030
Everyone says that.

243
00:12:21,130 --> 00:12:22,830
But how is it different than eating an animal?

244
00:12:23,310 --> 00:12:26,710
If you eat monsters, you'll get a weird disease and then transform into one.

245
00:12:26,810 --> 00:12:27,710
So no thank you!

246
00:12:28,210 --> 00:12:31,570
Things would be so much easier if that was something that actually happened.

247
00:12:31,570 --> 00:12:37,330
Monsters are believed to be unclean, and it's obviously not entirely logical, but that's

248
00:12:37,330 --> 00:12:40,110
the reason most people, including me, find it gross.

249
00:12:40,650 --> 00:12:43,230
You just get this feeling that you'll absorb something bad.

250
00:12:43,710 --> 00:12:48,250
New diseases spring up from creatures coming in contact with humans all the time, so it's

251
00:12:48,250 --> 00:12:51,050
not fair to question why someone doesn't feel like eating monsters.

252
00:12:51,830 --> 00:12:52,310
Mmm!

253
00:12:54,430 --> 00:12:55,670
This is really tasty!

254
00:12:56,450 --> 00:12:59,190
By the way, when you had to eat food you didn't like...

255
00:12:59,190 --> 00:13:01,270
How did you go about handling that exactly?

256
00:13:02,530 --> 00:13:03,730
What did I do?

257
00:13:06,310 --> 00:13:06,870
Ugh.

258
00:13:10,230 --> 00:13:11,890
Here, Tade, you can have this.

259
00:13:12,930 --> 00:13:13,890
Thanks, Isu!

260
00:13:14,410 --> 00:13:15,430
Me nice to be!

261
00:13:15,750 --> 00:13:17,110
That never happened.

262
00:13:17,410 --> 00:13:18,550
There's no way!

263
00:13:18,790 --> 00:13:19,350
Come on, you two!

264
00:13:19,510 --> 00:13:19,990
Let's go!

265
00:13:19,990 --> 00:13:33,830
This storm probably won't die down any time soon.

266
00:13:34,070 --> 00:13:36,130
Then let's set up camp around this area.

267
00:13:36,490 --> 00:13:37,630
I'm getting hungry.

268
00:13:38,450 --> 00:13:39,790
But Senshi fell asleep.

269
00:13:40,630 --> 00:13:42,270
We can prep a meal in the meantime.

270
00:13:43,130 --> 00:13:44,850
What ingredients do we have left?

271
00:13:44,850 --> 00:13:49,750
There's nightmares and a mandrake, eggs and some mushrooms, whatever this is.

272
00:13:49,810 --> 00:13:50,530
Got any fish?

273
00:13:50,770 --> 00:13:51,150
Nope.

274
00:13:51,330 --> 00:13:52,270
We're all out of that.

275
00:13:52,570 --> 00:13:53,230
Rice, then?

276
00:13:53,650 --> 00:13:56,050
We're actually pretty low on rice as well.

277
00:13:56,450 --> 00:13:58,810
Don't you have anything better than this gross stuff?

278
00:13:58,950 --> 00:13:59,910
This is everything.

279
00:14:00,250 --> 00:14:00,730
Liar!

280
00:14:00,990 --> 00:14:02,150
You're hiding it from me.

281
00:14:02,370 --> 00:14:04,770
You can't be a picky eater when you're inside a dungeon.

282
00:14:05,090 --> 00:14:06,850
So you should get used to trying things.

283
00:14:06,930 --> 00:14:07,310
No!

284
00:14:07,610 --> 00:14:09,390
I only eat the things I want to eat!

285
00:14:09,630 --> 00:14:10,790
Please just listen.

286
00:14:11,050 --> 00:14:13,270
Eating monsters isn't going to turn you into one.

287
00:14:13,270 --> 00:14:16,830
Do people who eat pigs and sheep turn into either of those animals?

288
00:14:17,650 --> 00:14:20,930
If someone who was blind ate an eyeball, would they regain their sight?

289
00:14:21,570 --> 00:14:24,230
Sheep only eat plants, but they stay sheep, don't they?

290
00:14:24,750 --> 00:14:27,870
Food and nutrition are more complex than you might think they are.

291
00:14:28,270 --> 00:14:30,610
That's why people are still conducting research.

292
00:14:30,830 --> 00:14:32,150
I'm sick of all your lies!

293
00:14:32,350 --> 00:14:33,990
How in the hell do you explain that, then?

294
00:14:34,310 --> 00:14:35,030
Explain what?

295
00:14:39,410 --> 00:14:41,510
A tree actually grew a sheep.

296
00:14:41,510 --> 00:14:43,350
That's a baromets.

297
00:14:43,590 --> 00:14:46,350
But to think it would actually show up at a time like this...

298
00:14:46,350 --> 00:14:49,370
So, first of all, that kind of plant is always like...

299
00:14:49,370 --> 00:14:49,790
Shut it!

300
00:14:50,150 --> 00:14:51,670
I'm sick of all your yammering!

301
00:14:52,130 --> 00:14:52,910
Whatever, man.

302
00:14:52,950 --> 00:14:54,150
I'm gonna go catch that sheep.

303
00:14:54,890 --> 00:14:56,150
What's a baromets?

304
00:14:56,270 --> 00:14:56,910
A monster?

305
00:14:57,490 --> 00:14:59,930
That's what it's classified as, but it's harmless.

306
00:15:00,370 --> 00:15:03,650
However, what's not harmless is they attract carnivores.

307
00:15:05,050 --> 00:15:06,190
Careful, Izutsumi!

308
00:15:06,190 --> 00:15:08,150
I don't need your warnings.

309
00:15:11,510 --> 00:15:12,310
And we shouldn't linger.

310
00:15:12,790 --> 00:15:13,890
Let's harvest it and then...

311
00:15:13,890 --> 00:15:14,210
Quiet.

312
00:15:15,170 --> 00:15:15,390
Huh?

313
00:15:19,870 --> 00:15:20,350
Crap!

314
00:15:20,550 --> 00:15:21,470
A direwolf pack!

315
00:15:21,470 --> 00:15:28,670
I need a staff!

316
00:15:33,670 --> 00:15:34,890
Hey, hold it!

317
00:15:35,310 --> 00:15:36,250
Where are you going?

318
00:15:36,850 --> 00:15:38,010
I'm not a fan of dogs.

319
00:15:38,150 --> 00:15:39,890
They're annoying and they smell bad.

320
00:15:40,810 --> 00:15:43,330
That's your reasoning for coming in here all on your own?

321
00:15:44,110 --> 00:15:45,570
I'm relying on them.

322
00:15:45,850 --> 00:15:49,810
Depending on your party members to pick up your slack is your idea of teamwork, isn't it?

323
00:15:49,810 --> 00:15:52,050
Uh, no, that's...

324
00:15:52,050 --> 00:15:53,350
That's not what that means at all!

325
00:15:53,390 --> 00:15:54,070
What do you mean?

326
00:15:54,270 --> 00:15:56,970
You didn't fight when we were dealing with that ice golem earlier.

327
00:15:57,570 --> 00:16:01,350
It's true I relied on you guys back then, but it wasn't because I didn't want to help out.

328
00:16:02,010 --> 00:16:04,770
Uh, hey, why don't we go back?

329
00:16:05,090 --> 00:16:05,690
No thanks.

330
00:16:05,690 --> 00:16:08,450
I smell fire on the wind.

331
00:16:08,710 --> 00:16:11,270
If we follow it, we'll get back to where we came from.

332
00:16:12,650 --> 00:16:13,850
Hey, wait up!

333
00:16:15,850 --> 00:16:20,170
The path to the right smells like the campfire, but it looks rough, so left it is.

334
00:16:20,430 --> 00:16:21,610
Do you know where you're going?

335
00:16:21,810 --> 00:16:22,870
Is this the right direction?

336
00:16:23,390 --> 00:16:25,370
I take whatever path I like the best.

337
00:16:25,690 --> 00:16:27,070
You should learn to do that, too.

338
00:16:27,610 --> 00:16:29,530
Why bother doing things you don't want to do?

339
00:16:29,530 --> 00:16:33,950
You eat monsters, even though you don't really want to eat them.

340
00:16:34,710 --> 00:16:36,010
It doesn't make any sense.

341
00:16:36,950 --> 00:16:38,730
Well, I mean...

342
00:16:38,730 --> 00:16:41,610
I think the wolves are coming after us.

343
00:16:41,930 --> 00:16:42,970
Should we try to fight them?

344
00:16:43,370 --> 00:16:47,470
I'm typically able to use explosive magic, but I don't have my staff right now.

345
00:16:47,690 --> 00:16:51,790
It's too cramped in here anyway, so I could stun them with a really bright light, maybe.

346
00:16:52,230 --> 00:16:53,390
Let's just lose them!

347
00:16:53,390 --> 00:16:58,010
Whoaaaa!

348
00:17:14,630 --> 00:17:15,230
Howie!

349
00:17:15,230 --> 00:17:24,050
Hey! Get back here, Asebi!

350
00:17:25,230 --> 00:17:28,530
Fess up. You made Tade shovel snow for you, didn't you?

351
00:17:29,250 --> 00:17:29,730
Nope.

352
00:17:30,230 --> 00:17:33,530
Don't lie to me! She fell off the training hall roof because of that!

353
00:17:33,770 --> 00:17:35,890
Unlike you, Tade is incredibly clumsy.

354
00:17:36,310 --> 00:17:38,390
So don't shove jobs you don't like onto her.

355
00:17:38,970 --> 00:17:41,010
Show some gratitude for us taking you in.

356
00:17:43,010 --> 00:17:43,490
Nah.

357
00:17:45,230 --> 00:17:45,930
Hey, Tade.

358
00:17:46,930 --> 00:17:49,170
Why'd you do something I never asked you for?

359
00:17:49,510 --> 00:17:50,410
You're such an idiot.

360
00:17:51,870 --> 00:17:53,230
But Tade just...

361
00:17:54,910 --> 00:17:57,650
What was it that Tade said to me back then?

362
00:17:58,950 --> 00:17:59,950
It doesn't matter.

363
00:18:05,390 --> 00:18:06,590
I messed up.

364
00:18:07,130 --> 00:18:10,530
The blast changed the wind's direction, so I missed this one.

365
00:18:10,530 --> 00:18:17,610
Cl-close your eyes.

366
00:18:18,610 --> 00:18:19,910
Close your eyes.

367
00:18:20,410 --> 00:18:20,970
Do it!

368
00:18:21,850 --> 00:18:22,310
Now!

369
00:18:22,310 --> 00:18:32,310
I can't...

370
00:18:32,310 --> 00:18:33,490
I... I can't...

371
00:18:33,490 --> 00:18:41,170
I... I...

372
00:18:41,170 --> 00:18:43,070
Is it Tade?

373
00:18:43,570 --> 00:18:44,630
Are you alive?

374
00:18:44,970 --> 00:18:45,910
Oh...

375
00:18:45,910 --> 00:18:50,610
Your arm is broken. Can you move? Let's go and find the others.

376
00:18:57,870 --> 00:19:02,270
Listen. You wanted to know why I eat monsters, didn't you?

377
00:19:03,050 --> 00:19:07,370
I've been thinking about it, and I have multiple goals that I want to accomplish.

378
00:19:07,950 --> 00:19:11,810
Like rescuing my best friend and learning everything I can about magic.

379
00:19:11,810 --> 00:19:18,430
So, while working to achieve all my goals, I sometimes run into things that I don't like.

380
00:19:18,830 --> 00:19:23,610
Something bothersome, or tiring, or having to eat something I really don't want to.

381
00:19:24,490 --> 00:19:27,810
None of those things are bad on their own, but...

382
00:19:28,370 --> 00:19:33,170
If I continued avoiding them, I'd keep getting further and further away from my path, right?

383
00:19:34,210 --> 00:19:36,090
Exactly like we're doing in this cave.

384
00:19:37,590 --> 00:19:40,770
I'm curious. Why did you decide to come along with us?

385
00:19:40,770 --> 00:19:47,150
Are you stupid? Because you told me I needed to find that mad whatever guy to even have a chance to break this curse!

386
00:19:47,490 --> 00:19:48,230
Now follow me!

387
00:19:48,970 --> 00:19:53,110
Exactly. And that means we probably won't be able to take the easy path there.

388
00:20:00,070 --> 00:20:02,670
Izutsumi! Marcil! You're both okay!

389
00:20:03,010 --> 00:20:04,850
You guys are okay too, right?

390
00:20:05,110 --> 00:20:07,330
Not really, but at least we're all in one piece.

391
00:20:07,330 --> 00:20:10,970
We have Laios' intimidation skills to thank for that.

392
00:20:11,130 --> 00:20:13,970
It helps that most of the wolves went after you, Marcil.

393
00:20:14,790 --> 00:20:15,390
You hurt?

394
00:20:15,910 --> 00:20:17,530
I think her arm is broken.

395
00:20:18,130 --> 00:20:21,650
Would you be able to help me out while I'm casting a healing spell on it, Laios?

396
00:20:21,650 --> 00:20:29,250
You did great, Izutsumi!

397
00:20:29,750 --> 00:20:32,190
The healing spell hurt more than breaking it.

398
00:20:32,710 --> 00:20:37,490
I was planning on harvesting the baromets, but all the ripe ones were taken by the dire wolves.

399
00:20:37,990 --> 00:20:40,770
This was the only one left for grabs, but it's not ready yet.

400
00:20:42,430 --> 00:20:43,770
Let's see if we can cook it.

401
00:20:43,770 --> 00:20:53,890
There's a little sheep inside the vegetable.

402
00:20:54,150 --> 00:20:54,950
I can't!

403
00:20:55,170 --> 00:20:57,850
For a completely different ethical reason, I refuse!

404
00:20:59,130 --> 00:21:02,650
First, cut up the baromets' ribs into whatever portions you want.

405
00:21:03,310 --> 00:21:04,890
Season them and put them on the fire.

406
00:21:05,610 --> 00:21:07,870
After both sides of each have been nicely browned,

407
00:21:08,090 --> 00:21:11,550
add wine over top, cover the pan, and then braise them.

408
00:21:11,550 --> 00:21:17,090
Next, boil the remainder of the fruit, peel off the skin, and cut it into chunks.

409
00:21:17,610 --> 00:21:19,850
Add some garlic and simmer all of it together.

410
00:21:20,470 --> 00:21:24,410
With the sauce finished, you take that, pour it over the meat, and...

411
00:21:24,410 --> 00:21:25,190
It's ready!

412
00:21:28,210 --> 00:21:29,770
This helping's yours, Catgirl.

413
00:21:30,110 --> 00:21:30,890
Go on, take it.

414
00:21:31,890 --> 00:21:33,730
What's all the weird-looking stuff?

415
00:21:34,010 --> 00:21:36,690
It's the skin of the baromets, fruit, and a handful of sprouts.

416
00:21:38,650 --> 00:21:41,430
You could have just fried the meat and been done with it.

417
00:21:41,550 --> 00:21:50,050
The baromets.

418
00:21:50,170 --> 00:21:51,950
It may resemble an everyday sheep,

419
00:21:52,150 --> 00:21:53,550
but it tastes more like crab!

420
00:21:53,690 --> 00:21:54,850
That doesn't make it better!

421
00:21:55,750 --> 00:21:57,090
This is so good.

422
00:21:57,310 --> 00:21:59,690
I didn't know something this delicious could exist.

423
00:22:00,690 --> 00:22:02,290
Wait, that reminds me.

424
00:22:03,050 --> 00:22:06,270
Tade, why'd you do something that I never asked you for?

425
00:22:07,230 --> 00:22:08,430
You're such an idiot.

426
00:22:09,570 --> 00:22:10,270
Tade just wants...

427
00:22:11,210 --> 00:22:13,850
to be as accommodating as she can to everyone.

428
00:22:15,170 --> 00:22:16,990
Because this place is amazing!

429
00:22:17,450 --> 00:22:18,350
Three meals a day,

430
00:22:18,550 --> 00:22:19,690
a bath to keep clean,

431
00:22:19,830 --> 00:22:20,970
and a cozy photon!

432
00:22:21,410 --> 00:22:23,770
I definitely cannot get myself kicked out of here!

433
00:22:24,010 --> 00:22:26,650
I will do even the smallest chore to show I'm useful!

434
00:22:26,650 --> 00:22:29,450
Hey, Asabi.

435
00:22:30,450 --> 00:22:33,450
Don't get discouraged just because of some minor inconveniences.

436
00:22:33,450 --> 00:22:38,090
Oh, and if I do good,

437
00:22:38,190 --> 00:22:40,290
Lady Miser will give me treats sometimes!

438
00:22:40,490 --> 00:22:42,490
So that's what you're really after, huh?

439
00:22:43,430 --> 00:22:44,950
Guess this is what she meant.

440
00:22:45,430 --> 00:22:48,330
Sometimes you get tasty things out of doing what you don't wanna.

441
00:22:48,330 --> 00:22:53,170
Good job!

442
00:22:53,290 --> 00:22:54,870
I'm proud of you, Izutsumi!

443
00:22:54,930 --> 00:22:56,170
You did so well today!

444
00:22:56,610 --> 00:22:57,570
Way to go, bud!

445
00:22:57,590 --> 00:22:58,950
Turn it out, you bastards!

446
00:22:59,190 --> 00:23:00,790
What do you think you're doing?!

447
00:23:00,790 --> 00:23:02,150
Don't touch me!

448
00:23:03,190 --> 00:23:05,590
I only ate it because I had no other choice!

449
00:23:05,830 --> 00:23:08,510
You'll never see me eat gross veggies or monsters again!

450
00:23:09,050 --> 00:23:11,670
You won't know if they're gross or not till you try them, though.

451
00:23:12,250 --> 00:23:13,110
By the way, Marcel,

452
00:23:13,430 --> 00:23:15,210
you've barely touched your food.

453
00:23:15,210 --> 00:23:17,530
After all the lecturing you gave me earlier,

454
00:23:17,650 --> 00:23:19,390
don't you even try to get out of eating.

455
00:23:20,830 --> 00:23:25,030
Marcel deeply regretted being the one to close off her own escape route.

456
00:23:25,810 --> 00:23:27,330
Ah, dungeon food.

457
00:23:27,670 --> 00:23:29,290
Delicious in dungeon.

